DO $$
DECLARE
  v_course_id uuid;
  v_module_id uuid;
  v_whatsapp_plan_id uuid;
BEGIN
  -- 1. Locate Course: mrcem-sba
  SELECT id INTO v_course_id FROM "courses" WHERE "slug" = 'mrcem-sba' LIMIT 1;
  IF v_course_id IS NULL THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Course mrcem-sba not found. Please ensure mrcem-sba exists before running this seed.';
  END IF;

  -- Module: Resuscitation & Critical Care
  SELECT id INTO v_module_id FROM "modules" WHERE "course_id" = v_course_id AND "title" = 'Resuscitation & Critical Care' AND "deleted_at" IS NULL LIMIT 1;
  IF v_module_id IS NULL THEN
    INSERT INTO "modules" ("id", "course_id", "title", "position", "created_at", "updated_at")
    VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), v_course_id, 'Resuscitation & Critical Care', 5, now(), now())
    RETURNING "id" INTO v_module_id;
  ELSE
    UPDATE "modules" SET "position" = 5, "updated_at" = now() WHERE "id" = v_module_id;
  END IF;

  -- Lesson: Brief Resolved Unexplained Event (BRUE)
  INSERT INTO "lessons" (
    "id", "module_id", "slug", "title", "type", "body", "is_free_preview", "position", "status", "created_at", "updated_at"
  ) VALUES (
    gen_random_uuid(),
    v_module_id,
    'brief-resolved-unexplained-event-brue',
    'Brief Resolved Unexplained Event (BRUE)',
    'article',
    $BODY$# Brief Resolved Unexplained Event (BRUE)

>lt's an episode in an infant less than 12 months of age characterized by: -<1 minute duration (typically 20-30s) >A return to baseline state >Not explained by any identifiable medical condition (i.e. medically well). >lncludes one or more of the following features: >CentraI cyanosis/pallor >Absent, decrease or irregular breathing >Marked change in tone (hyper- or hypotonia) >Altered level of consciousness -Differential diagnosis >Gastro-esophageal reflux >infection >EpiIepsy >Non-accidental injury >Arrythmias (long QT) >Myocarditis >Metabolic error

- Always take complete history from parents or eye witnessed including general description of event eg: choking gagging , last feed. -Gestational history, social history, family history. -Examination >ABCDE assessment >exposure check for bruising, bleeding from nose/mouth, torn frenulum and subconjunctival hemorrhage. >measure weight, length and head circumference >Any dysmorphic features that might indicate underlying congenital abnormalities -Note: always documents any normal or negative finding in examination such as Mongolian blue spot. -Risk stratification —Investigation & management Gastro-esophageal reflux disease >lt's one of the commonest causes of symptoms similar to a BRUE presentation, causing symptoms via laryngospasm. It is an important one to exclude as it is a very treatable cause of a presentation similar to a BRUE, and may cause repeated episodes. -Features from the history that are suggestive of it are:

-
-
- Low risk days of age Born >32 weeks' gestation and have a corrected age of >45 weeks. No CPR given by trained practitioner <1 minute duration First event
-
- High risk Infant< 2 months Hx Of prematurity less than 32 weeks at birth More than one event >Episode occurred whilst infant was awake and supine >Occurred during feeding or shortly after feeding >Regurgitation or vomiting at time of event >Obstructive apnea (infant making respiratory efforts but not breathing successfully). -Note: Always consider NAI (e.g: drug ingestion, factitious illness, suffocation), especially if there are multiple or changing versions of the history.

Low risk
- Investigation: May obtain pertussis testing and 12 lead ECG. Briefly monitor with pulse oximetry. Management: Educate caregiver abt BRUE and engage in shared decision & follow- up. Offer resources and CPR training previOUS  Next High risk Investigation: For high risk patients do a capillary blood gas and ECG as a minimum, and keep these patients on a cardiorespiratory monitor. Management: Referral to Paediatrics for a 24-hour period of monitoring +/- investigations.

