    'transfction-mangement-of-major-hge',
    'Transfction Mangement of Major Hge',
    'article',
    $BODY$# Transfction Mangement of Major Hge

- Ptbleeding/collapsed or in clinical shock
- Trigger the major blood loss protocol
- If trauma and <3hrs from injury, give tranexamic acid lg bolus over IO minutes followed by infusion of lg over 8hr (Consider tranexamic acid lg bolus in non-traumatic Pt)
- Take baseline blood sample for: Cross-match, FBC, clotting screen, fibrinogen level, IJ&E and Calcium level Give initial MHP-1which include 4 or 6 units RBC 4 units Add 1 dose of plt in trauma patients earlier Reassess the Pt If require further transfusion then take baseline sample for: FBC, clotting screen, fibrinogen level, I-J&E and Calcium level Order MHP-2 which include 4-6 units of RBC, 4units of FFP, I dose of plt 2 packs of cryoprecipitate Transfusion of MHP-2 depends on lab results eg: if Hb in lab value <8 then transfuse RBC otherwise not
- Aim to maintain following
- values PLT PT ratio APTT ratio Fibrinogen Ca2+ 8-1 Ogldl X 109 IL >1.5gn > lmmol/l

- Repeat the baseline investigation which include: > FBC, clotting screen, fibrinogen level, IJ&E and Calcium level Correct complications: hypocalcaemia, hypothermia, acidosis  Next

