Amsel Criteria for Diagnosis of BV: Three of the following four criteria must be met. Establishes accurate diagnosis of bacterial vaginosis in 90% of affected women. 1) Homogeneous, non-clumping vaginal discharge (color and amount may vary) 2) Amine (fishy) odor when potassium hydroxide solution is added to vaginal secretions (commonly called the "whiff test") 3) Presence of clue cells (greater than 20%) on microscopy 4) Vaginal pH greater than 4-5

