  INSERT INTO "lessons" (
    "id", "module_id", "slug", "title", "type", "body", "is_free_preview", "position", "status", "created_at", "updated_at"
  ) VALUES (
    gen_random_uuid(),
    v_module_id,
    'acute-myocarditis',
    'Acute Myocarditis',
    'article',
    $BODY$# Acute Myocarditis

### Definition

- Myocarditis is an acute infectious or immunologically mediated syndrome causing inflammation of the heart muscle.
- The histological dead myocytes with surrounding inflammatory infiltrates.
- Cause
- Virus Cocksackie (most common)
- Adenovirus Influenza
- Parainfluenza
- Mumps
- Rubella
- Varicella zoster
-
- Epstein Barr Rabies
-
- CMV Bacteria
- Lyme disease
- Mycobacteria Mycoplasma Legionella
- Streptococcus species
-
- Chlamydia pneumonia

- Parasite-I-Eungi Aspergillus
-
- Cryptococcus Candida
- Trypanosoma cruzi — Chagas disease
- Toxoplasmosis
- Schistosomiasis
- Trichinosis
- Drugs-a-toxinslother TCA Sulphonamide
- Cephalosporin
- Vaccination
- Metal toxin
- Cocaine
- Immunological
-
- Clinical features Pt presents with chest pain and 90% of them has a history of viral prodrome illness
- such as UPRTI or gastroenteritis (sore throat, vomiting, diarrhea. Most Pt are young blow 50 years
-
- Investigation

ECG
- CXR to check pulmonary oedema, cardiomegaly. Etc
- ECHO to check ejection fraction, dilated heart or pericardial effusion.
- FBC, U&E, CRP/ESR ,
- Troponin/creatinine kinase elevated but can be normal
- EndomyocardiaLbiopsy_is the Cold standard for diagnosis of myocarditis
- Management Haemodynamically stable: no evidence of LV systolic dysfunction
-
- Haemodynamically stable: evidence of left ventricular systolic dysfunction Haemodynamically unstable: adults Haemodynamically unstable: children End-stage heart failure or refractory life-threatening arrhythmias
-
-
-
-
- First line - supportive care ± treatment of underlying cause depends on the cause if autoimmune then methylprednisolone etc. Consider IVIG First line - ACE inhibitor (e.g., captopril, enalapril, lisinopril) or angiotensin-II receptor antagonist (e.g., candesartan, valsartan). Consider IVIG and treat underlying cause Consider diuretics and beta blockers (in selected patients only) First line - arterial vasodilator (Sodium nitroprusside) + invasive haemodynamic monitoring Consider IVIG, GTN, inotropes or vesopressors First line — inotropes (milrinone or dobutamine) Consider IVIG and mechanical circulatory support First line - Heart transplantation

previous  Next

