>Most common 10 renal malignancy C >Most common in males 50—70 years old >lncrease incidence with tobacco smoking and obesity. >Originate from PCT —Clinical features >Classic triad : >flank pain >palpable mass >hematuria >Other feature (fever, polycythemia, weight-loss) -Investigation : CT scan Z.Manageme.nt;-surgical intervention , immunotherapy eg:ipilimumab -Bladder carcinoma (transitional cells carcinoma or Urothelial carcinoma of the bladder) >Most common tumor of urinary tract system (can occur in renal calyces, renal pelvis, ureters and bladder) -Clinical feature

>Painless haematuria (no casts) >Associated with Phenacetin, tobacco Smoking, Aromatic amines (found in dyes), Cyclophosphamide. Pneumonic (Pee SAC) -Investigation : Cystoscopy and CT -Management: chemotherapy and surgical intervention previous  Next

