25/11/2025, 10:17 paper - II I MRCEM EXPERT LLC Which of these is a complication specifically of massive transfusion? A
- Thrombotic events
- **B)** Metabolic acidosis   C Hypocalcemia
- **D)** ABO incompatibility
- **E)** Blood borne virus transmission Explanatign Complications of massive transfusion Hypothermia - is a complication of massive transfusion. The rapid infusion of cold blood products can lower body temperatures. The use of warmers can reduce this risk.
- Hyperkalemia - is a complication of massive transfusion. Stored blood products can accumulate higher concentrations of potassium. Hypokalemia cannot be attributed to massive transfusion.
