- Suxamethonium is metabolised by an enzyme in the blood called plasma cholinesterase. Metabolism is normally complete within 5-10 minutes. Suxamethonium action prolong with cholinesterase inhibitors or those patients who lack this enzyme (cholinesterase) or have an altered enzyme that does not metabolise the suxamethonium as rapidly. These patients may remain paralysed for many hours after a standard dose of suxamethonium, and must be kept anaesthetised and ventilated until the suxamethonium has been eliminated by other, slower methods. 84 / 90

