- Use 10% estimate for deficit calculation (Note: use 10% estimate for deficit calculation shock patient and 5% in non-shock patients, to assess that, check table-A in assessment) Body weight ISt 10kg 2nd 10kg 3rd 10kg Daily/per-day fluid requirements 100ml/kg 50ml/kg 20ml/kg Hourly fluid requirement 4ml/kg 2ml/kg Iml/kg

- Example -1 A 26 kg child responded to a 20 ml/kg or 10ml/kg (follow resus) fluid bolus and is no longer shocked. Calculate fluid deficit? formula: %age x weight x IO IO x 26 x IO = 2600mI (replace in 24-48 hrs)
- Example-2 A 26 kg child responded to a 20 ml/kg or 10mI/kg (follow resus) fluid bolus and is no longer shocked. What is his maintenance hourly IV fluid requirement using the standard regime? Hourly maintenance = (10kg x 4mI) + (10kg x 2mI) + (6kg x Imi) = 66mI/hr if convert to daily maintenance = (100 ml/kg x IO kg) + (50 ml/kg x IO kg) + (20 ml/kg x 6 kg) 1620ml/day
