Fit an appropriately sized semi-rigid collar unless contraindicated by: o a compromised airway o known spinal deformities, such as ankylosing spondylitis (in these cases keep the spine in the person's current position). Reassess the airway after applying the collar. Place and secure the person on a scoop stretcher. Secure the person with head blocks and tape, ideally in a vacuum mattress. When carrying out full in-line spinal immobilisation in children, further consider: o involving family members and carers if appropriate o keeping infants in their car seat if possible o using a scoop stretcher with blanket rolls, vacuum mattress, vacuum limb splints or Kendrick extrication device.
