- In the emergency department, administer prophylactic intravenous antibiotics immediately to people with open fractures if not already given. 10 / 12 IO. A 50-year-old male patient with laryngectomy in situ brought to the ED with complain of dizziness, vomiting. One of your junior colleague has passed NG tube. To confirm NG tube, x-ray was done which is shown. What would be your next step?
