- The gastroduodenal junction is located just to the right side of the midline (spine indicates midline)
- To ensure the tube is not in the duodenum, its tip is ideally placed more proximally in the stomach to the left of the midline. However in this X-ray NG tube in the right side of midline and it's in the duodenum, therefore, for feeding into the stomach this tube should be withdrawn and its position confirmed either by a further attempt of aspiration of gastric fluid or by repeating the X-ray.
