- maximal inspiratory pressure worse than -30 cmH20
- maximal expiratory pressure <40 cmH20; or reduction of 30% or more
- of vital capacity, maximal inspiratory pressure, or maximal expiratory pressure. Note - The key diagnostic tests for the ED are the lumbar puncture,
